WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:03.202
 Bobby, Will,
congratulations, you

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:04.871
guys are in the third and final
round of this competition.

00:00:04.938 --> 00:00:07.172
When you came here, you
tore down our Great Wall

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.476
to make your signature
blades that have propelled

00:00:09.576 --> 00:00:10.877
you into this third round.

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:12.478
And now, it's time
for a little payback

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:14.247
as we send you back
to your home forges

00:00:14.313 --> 00:00:17.650
to recreate this iconic
weapon from history.

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:18.918
You ready to see what it is?

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:19.652
 Yes, sir.

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:20.786
 Yes. sir.

00:00:20.886 --> 00:00:21.954
 All right, that weapon is--

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:25.091
[intense music]

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:26.559
--the Chinese war sword.

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:27.426
 Ooh.

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:29.929
[blade clanking]

00:00:29.995 --> 00:00:30.763
 All right, gents.

00:00:30.863 --> 00:00:31.797
Do your best work.

00:00:31.864 --> 00:00:32.699
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:33.666
 Thank you, sir.

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:34.567
 Good luck.

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:35.301
 Good luck to you, too.

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:38.404 line:7%
[rock music]

00:00:38.504 --> 00:00:41.307
It's day one, back in
Hodgenville at the home forge.

00:00:41.373 --> 00:00:42.876
I've got a Chinese
war sword to make.

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:44.343
This thing is huge.

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:45.978
All my forging is
done by hand, so it's

00:00:46.078 --> 00:00:47.380
going to be a challenge.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:50.316
I'm starting off with a
piece of 51-60 Spring steel,

00:00:50.382 --> 00:00:53.019
and I've got a lot
of metal to move.

00:00:53.085 --> 00:00:55.154
That's going to take a minute.

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:57.389
Normally, I like to
forge the tang first,

00:00:57.456 --> 00:00:59.125
so I'm going to
lay on my shoulders

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:02.328
and start getting my tang
drawn out to its final length.

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:07.099
I'm working my way up the blade,
and the hammer head falls off.

00:01:07.199 --> 00:01:08.434
Luckily, I've got
plenty of hammers,

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:11.404
so I knock a handle off
and put a old cross pein

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:13.406
head on this one.

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:15.441
And the second
cross pein's broken.

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:17.977
And all I have is a 6
and 1/2 pound sledge.

00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:20.046
So "Forged in Fire" stars,
that's when the hammers

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:21.581
start falling apart.

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:25.885 line:0%
Right now, I'm really missing
the press in the judges' forge.

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:27.720 line:0%
 There is an
extremely long list

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:29.022 line:7%
of things to get done today.

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:31.891
A quench would just be a
blessing all the way around.

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:33.259
Let's get cracking.

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:35.094
One of the iconic
features of this sword

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:37.697
is it has a hole up on
the pierced clip point

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:40.432
that you always take the
chance of creating a crack

00:01:40.532 --> 00:01:42.401
when you're drilling
that close to the edge.

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:45.538
That made it a
whole lot lighter.

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:47.506
Now, it's time to
do the heat treat.

00:01:47.573 --> 00:01:51.877
I fill up my quench tube
with fresh quench oil.

00:01:51.944 --> 00:01:54.547
I got my blade heated up.

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:56.215
I get my blade.

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:58.618
That can go straight
into the jig.

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:01.487
I've got a fully quenched
Chinese war sword.

00:02:01.587 --> 00:02:02.655
Oh!

00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:03.823
Thank you, lord.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:05.224 line:0%
I wanna let it
temper tonight, and

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:06.959 line:0%
tomorrow, I'm ready to
start on the handle,

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:10.029 line:7%
and keep moving forward.

00:02:10.129 --> 00:02:12.030 line:7%
 I've got a lot of work to do.

00:02:12.131 --> 00:02:13.165
First thing I've
got to do today is

00:02:13.265 --> 00:02:15.067
start drawing out this blade.

00:02:15.134 --> 00:02:16.903
It's nowhere near
the parameters,

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:19.038
but I did repair my
cross pein hammer,

00:02:19.138 --> 00:02:21.407
so hopefully, that holds up.

00:02:21.473 --> 00:02:24.176
Right now, I'm drawing out
at about an inch an hour.

00:02:24.243 --> 00:02:25.945
I've got, like, 20
minutes left today.

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:26.779
And--

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:28.347
Oh, [bleep].

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:32.684
--a huge crack has opened
up behind my ricasso.

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:34.654
That's not good.

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:39.125
I have developed a major
crack right at the most

00:02:39.191 --> 00:02:41.928
vulnerable point in my handle.

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:44.163
My gut reaction is
to jump on the welder

00:02:44.229 --> 00:02:46.532
and seal up this
crack the best I can.

00:02:46.598 --> 00:02:49.636
But I might be able to think
of a better way to repair this,

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:52.838
so I'm going to just stop and
try to come at this problem

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:54.707
again tomorrow.

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:59.011 line:0%
This crack is just going to
be over my head all night.

00:02:59.077 --> 00:03:00.847 line:7%
It's the morning of day four.

00:03:00.913 --> 00:03:03.282 line:0%
Now, I'm ready to start
putting an edge on this blade.

00:03:03.382 --> 00:03:05.818
This is an extremely long
blade, so it's going to be

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:07.620
a challenge to sharpen this.

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:08.721
I got an edge put on it.

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:10.956
I want to test my edge
geometry and see if it's

00:03:11.023 --> 00:03:12.524
the edge I'm looking for.

00:03:12.624 --> 00:03:16.095
So we're going to try just a
simple gallon jug slice here.

00:03:16.195 --> 00:03:18.030
I get a good, smooth, clean cut.

00:03:18.096 --> 00:03:19.965
There's no issues, no problems.

00:03:20.032 --> 00:03:21.099
Good deal.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.801
The leather wrap
is the way to go.

00:03:22.901 --> 00:03:25.304
I don't want this handle to have
any chance of coming undone.

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:28.807
I am gluing this
one wrap at a time.

00:03:28.907 --> 00:03:30.143
It actually looks pretty good.

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:31.644
I'm done.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:32.811
A little bit nervous.

00:03:32.911 --> 00:03:34.247
I'd be lying if I said I wasn't.

00:03:34.314 --> 00:03:37.149
But the excitement is much
more than anything else.

00:03:37.216 --> 00:03:39.885 line:7%
[rock music]

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:41.320 line:7%
 It's day four.

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:44.090
I'm going to have to MIG
weld this crack to keep

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:45.591
it from getting any worse.

00:03:45.691 --> 00:03:48.661
Then I'm going to create a
mechanically connected san mai.

00:03:48.761 --> 00:03:51.697
I'm gonna take two
pieces of mild steel,

00:03:51.797 --> 00:03:54.667
and weld them and rivet
them onto the sides

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:56.202
to create a new handle.

00:03:56.268 --> 00:03:57.203
They're going to be my guards.

00:03:57.269 --> 00:03:58.638
They're going to be my pommel.

00:03:58.738 --> 00:04:00.105
And they're going to
make sure my blade

00:04:00.205 --> 00:04:02.408
doesn't break into two pieces.

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:04.877
With the remaining
time left, I've gotta

00:04:04.977 --> 00:04:06.945
get started making this handle.

00:04:07.012 --> 00:04:08.381
I slap these handles on.

00:04:08.447 --> 00:04:10.383
They're gluing up.

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:11.751
Whoo!

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:16.122
This has been the longest and
shortest four days of my life.

00:04:16.189 --> 00:04:18.358
I wish I had more time
to focus on the details.

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:22.028
But at the end of the day, it
meets parameters, it's safe,

00:04:22.094 --> 00:04:24.963
and it functions.

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:25.998
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:04:26.098 --> 00:04:28.501
Welcome to the kill test.

00:04:28.567 --> 00:04:32.471
To find out what kind of lethal
damage your weapon will do,

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:33.773
I will take your
Chinese war sword

00:04:33.839 --> 00:04:37.543
and deliver one strike
on this ram carcass.

00:04:37.643 --> 00:04:39.445
Let's see how deadly they are.

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:40.913
Bobby, you're first.
You ready for this?

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:41.680
 Yes, sir.

00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:43.716
 Let's do this.

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:46.285
 My heart's just
bouncing out of my chest.

00:04:46.385 --> 00:04:47.252
You've got the skin.

00:04:47.319 --> 00:04:48.087
You've got the bones.

00:04:48.154 --> 00:04:49.354
You've got the hide.

00:04:49.421 --> 00:04:52.791
I only get one shot
at this ram carcass?

00:04:52.891 --> 00:04:56.362
[rock music]

00:05:08.006 --> 00:05:09.609
 All right, Bobby.

00:05:09.676 --> 00:05:10.876
One and done.

00:05:10.943 --> 00:05:14.379
As much as this is very
intimidating in its look,

00:05:14.446 --> 00:05:16.215
it is crafted nicely.

00:05:16.315 --> 00:05:18.651
It's got a beautiful
look to its finish.

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:21.653
The balance, it's just right
for a two-handed sword.

00:05:21.753 --> 00:05:23.355
A little forward-heavy,
but that tells

00:05:23.455 --> 00:05:25.124
you that's where the power is.

00:05:25.191 --> 00:05:26.525
Your edge is sharp.

00:05:26.625 --> 00:05:29.361
Even cutting through the
spine and bones, no issues,

00:05:29.428 --> 00:05:30.896
no glinting, and no rolls.

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:36.135
Overall, sir, your Chinese
war sword will kill.

00:05:36.202 --> 00:05:37.536
 Thank you, sir.

00:05:37.603 --> 00:05:38.771
 All right, Will, your turn.

00:05:38.838 --> 00:05:39.572
Ready?
- Yes, sir.

00:05:39.639 --> 00:05:40.005
I'm ready.

00:05:40.106 --> 00:05:41.273
 Let's do this.

00:05:41.374 --> 00:05:44.076
[music playing]

00:05:44.176 --> 00:05:45.611
 Doug picks up my weapon.

00:05:45.677 --> 00:05:47.714
And at this point, all the
nerves are out the window.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:48.814
I'm just excited.

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:50.282
He's walking towards
this ram's carcass,

00:05:50.382 --> 00:05:52.618
and I'm ready to see
it fly right through.

00:05:52.718 --> 00:05:54.020
[exhales]

00:05:54.087 --> 00:05:57.490
[music playing]

00:06:02.761 --> 00:06:04.630
 (WHISPERING) Good job, buddy.

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:05.764
 Thank you.

00:06:05.865 --> 00:06:08.501
[music playing]

00:06:08.567 --> 00:06:09.768
 All right, Will.

00:06:09.835 --> 00:06:11.536
Let's talk about your
Chinese war sword here.

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:14.306
First up, it's a
very bulky handle.

00:06:14.407 --> 00:06:15.808
It's rounded.

00:06:15.875 --> 00:06:19.011
So as you get a good grip on
it, you can feel it starts

00:06:19.078 --> 00:06:20.379
to spread my hands around.

00:06:20.446 --> 00:06:22.581
But the wrapping that
you put around it does

00:06:22.681 --> 00:06:25.818
allow me to get a good grip
on it, so good on that.

00:06:25.885 --> 00:06:27.553
And one shot, one kill.

00:06:27.653 --> 00:06:30.656
Overall, sir, your
weapon, it will kill.

00:06:30.757 --> 00:06:32.191
 Thank you, sir.

00:06:32.291 --> 00:06:34.560
 Oh, I just felt a
frightening chill.

00:06:34.627 --> 00:06:36.128
Must be the strength test.

00:06:36.228 --> 00:06:36.929
J?

00:06:40.032 --> 00:06:41.233
 You boys remember me.

00:06:41.333 --> 00:06:42.167
 Yes, sir.

00:06:42.234 --> 00:06:43.235
 Yes, sir.

00:06:43.301 --> 00:06:44.537
 Welcome to the ice block chop.

00:06:47.006 --> 00:06:49.341
This is going to test not only
your edge in your heat treat,

00:06:49.441 --> 00:06:52.444
but the overall
construction of your swords.

00:06:52.544 --> 00:06:54.313
Now, what your
blades do to the ice,

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:55.815
I'm not too concerned about.

00:06:55.882 --> 00:06:58.116
I want to see what the ice
is gonna do to your blades.

00:06:58.183 --> 00:06:59.118
Bobby, you're up first.

00:06:59.218 --> 00:07:00.819
How are you feeling?

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:01.587
 Ready to go.

00:07:01.654 --> 00:07:02.220
 Me too.

00:07:02.287 --> 00:07:03.723
Let's do it.

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:05.124
[intense music]

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:06.492
This is not just an ice block.

00:07:06.592 --> 00:07:08.261
This thing's a glacier.

00:07:08.327 --> 00:07:10.463
J can't wait to start
swinging that thing.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:13.832
He's going to do it with
everything he has in him.

00:07:13.899 --> 00:07:17.803
I just don't know how
it's going to hold up.

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:20.706
[rock music]

00:07:21.774 --> 00:07:25.111
 [grunting]

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:47.199
Great job, Bobby.

00:07:47.299 --> 00:07:48.367
Still razor sharp.

00:07:48.467 --> 00:07:51.103
No rolls, no glints, nothing.

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:52.804
Everything's still tight.

00:07:52.904 --> 00:07:56.408
I mean, one of the swings, I
was able to split that block.

00:07:56.475 --> 00:07:58.176
So it's got a good feel.

00:07:58.243 --> 00:07:59.978
Just nice job overall.

00:08:00.045 --> 00:08:01.079
 Thank you.

00:08:01.179 --> 00:08:02.882
 OK, Will, how are you feeling?

00:08:02.948 --> 00:08:05.251
 [laughs] I'm nervous,
but I'm excited.

00:08:05.351 --> 00:08:06.184
 OK.

00:08:06.251 --> 00:08:07.018
I'm just excited, so--

00:08:07.119 --> 00:08:09.154
[music playing]

00:08:09.221 --> 00:08:10.689
 This is going to be brutal.

00:08:10.756 --> 00:08:12.991
I'm really worried about the
crack in my tang right now.

00:08:13.058 --> 00:08:16.295 line:0%
Chopping through a block
that big is so tough.

00:08:16.395 --> 00:08:19.098
If there are any
compromises in my blade,

00:08:19.165 --> 00:08:21.133
this is where they're
going to show their head.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:22.134
[exhales]

00:08:32.144 --> 00:08:33.011
[grunts]

00:08:33.078 --> 00:08:34.580
[clanging]

00:08:37.416 --> 00:08:40.520
[music playing]

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:49.461
 Well, we got a problem, Will.

00:08:49.528 --> 00:08:50.863
 A big problem, sir.

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:53.598
 Right where you did your
very rough hollow grind,

00:08:53.698 --> 00:08:56.535
there's a couple dark
spots right in here.

00:08:56.601 --> 00:08:58.136
And with that thin
spot right there,

00:08:58.203 --> 00:09:00.572
it was enough to allow that
blade to just snap right

00:09:00.672 --> 00:09:02.574
in half on the first swing.

00:09:02.674 --> 00:09:07.078
So it did not survive,
but good effort.

00:09:07.179 --> 00:09:07.813
 Thank you, sir.

00:09:11.417 --> 00:09:12.985
 Well, Will, sometimes
this competition's

00:09:13.085 --> 00:09:15.187
full of tough breaks,
and you've had one

00:09:15.287 --> 00:09:19.525
on the first strike against this
ice block in our strength test.

00:09:19.592 --> 00:09:22.394
Unfortunately, we cannot
continue testing your blade

00:09:22.461 --> 00:09:24.063
against your opponent's.

00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:26.565
And for that reason, I'd like to
invite you to shake our hands,

00:09:26.632 --> 00:09:28.700
shake your opponent's
hand, and then please

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:30.169
leave the forge to your right.

00:09:30.269 --> 00:09:30.936
Come on, my friend.

00:09:31.003 --> 00:09:32.137
 Yes, sir.

00:09:32.204 --> 00:09:33.272
 Excellent work, dude.

00:09:33.372 --> 00:09:35.841
 Thank you, brother.

00:09:35.908 --> 00:09:36.942
It's tough.

00:09:37.042 --> 00:09:38.711
Having a blade break is
obviously-- you know,

00:09:38.811 --> 00:09:40.179
it's a tremendous failure.

00:09:40.246 --> 00:09:43.148
But at the end of the day,
I did the best I could

00:09:43.215 --> 00:09:44.550
with the tools I had.

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:47.519
And I'm still proud of the
piece that I put forward.

00:09:47.619 --> 00:09:50.189
This competition has
given me the inspiration

00:09:50.289 --> 00:09:55.894
to move forward and
challenge myself in new ways.

00:09:55.961 --> 00:09:58.063
 Bobby, you are the
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:58.130 --> 00:10:00.633
And that's a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:10:00.699 --> 00:10:01.433
Good job, brother.

00:10:01.533 --> 00:10:02.768
[applause]

00:10:02.868 --> 00:10:05.604
Come on forward, my friend.

00:10:05.704 --> 00:10:06.972
Great job.
Great work.

00:10:07.039 --> 00:10:07.939
 Thank you.

00:10:08.006 --> 00:10:09.241
I feel on top of
the world right now.

00:10:09.341 --> 00:10:10.175
 That's a great piece, man.

00:10:10.242 --> 00:10:11.243
That was fun to swing.

00:10:11.343 --> 00:10:12.811
 This is not just a win for me.

00:10:12.878 --> 00:10:16.515
This is a win for my family,
my friends, the other smiths

00:10:16.582 --> 00:10:18.484
that I teach in the forge.

00:10:18.551 --> 00:10:20.452
This goes a long ways
for our whole community.

00:10:20.519 --> 00:10:23.889
[music playing]

